cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IoTiX, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "IoTiX: A Mobile-Native Visual Programming Language for the Internet of Things"
abstract: >-
  The growth of the Internet of Things (IoT) is slowed by tools not designed
  for non-programmers on mobile devices. Existing solutions trade off
  usability and expressivity: trigger-action approaches like IFTTT sacrifice
  expressivity for ease of use, while visual languages like Blockly can be
  cumbersome on small screens. We present IoTiX: a mobile-first visual
  programming language that blends block-based and form-based paradigms and
  is powered by a dynamic metamodel that adapts constructs to selected
  devices, restricting users to valid, compatible actions. Validated through
  user studies and a pilot deployment in Logimic, IoTiX reduces the gap
  between usability and expressive power, enabling non-trivial IoT
  automations.
